.TH RUN-SUPPLIER 1 "2026-11-08" "cti-agent 1.6" "CTI Fleet Manual"
.SH NAME
run-supplier \- supplier-request lane: judge each new supplier request, file a Kanban item for the critical or unsure ones, email one digest
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B run\-supplier
.RB ( \-\-dry\-run | \-\-for\-real | \-\-to\-dev )
.PP
.B sudo cti\-agent run\-supplier
.RB ( \-\-dry\-run | \-\-for\-real | \-\-to\-dev )
.SH DESCRIPTION
The shared mailbox is on the supplier-request distribution list.
.B run-supplier
runs
.BR cti\-supplier (1)
to find each new request (a conversation with
.B SUPPLIER_ADDRESS
in To or Cc) and read it: the message text and the supplier request form, never
the W\-9 or bank attachments. Each request is judged against one question: will
this supplier touch company data, systems or networks, or provide technology? A
Yes means the supplier is critical and has to go through third\-party risk
management; a No is a supplier of materials or other non\-technology goods.
.PP
A Yes or an Unsure gets an item on the security team's Kanban board (Jira
project
.BR SUPPLIER_JIRA_PROJECT ).
An Unsure is treated as critical: it means the lane could not determine a
certain Yes, so a person has to look. A No gets no item and appears in the digest
only. One digest email goes to the security team, pointing at the board, and a
day with no new requests sends nothing.
.SS The model
With
.B SUPPLIER_MODEL
set, each request is shown to a Claude session started with no tools, no MCP
servers, no session file and no settings from the host. It reads one file and
writes one JSON object. Its instructions are in
.BR agents/supplier/CLAUDE.md .
.BR cti\-supplier (1)
then checks every claim against the request and only ever moves an answer toward
Unsure: a Yes or No needs a quote copied from the request; a No is refused when
the form was not read, when the name or notes hold a technology word, or when the
request tried to steer the reader.
.PP
With
.B SUPPLIER_MODEL
unset, or the model missing or down, or its output unusable, a request is Unsure.
The lane degrades toward asking a person, never toward a No.
.PP
Recipients are
.BR SUPPLIER_TO ,
checked against
.BR SUPPLIER_ALLOW_TO ,
neither of which has a fallback: unset means the mailer refuses. It is run by
.B cti\-agent\-supplier.service
as
.B run\-supplier \-\-for\-real
from
.BR cti\-agent\-supplier.timer ,
daily at 07:45 local (the installer pins it to
.B FLEET_TIMEZONE
with
.BR FLEET_SUPPLIER_TIME ).
It is off until enabled, and does nothing until
.B SUPPLIER_ADDRESS
is set.
.SH HOW TO RUN
\fBrun\-supplier\fR files tickets and mails a digest, so it has no default: it has to be told how to run. Give exactly one of
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR (judge and render; file nothing, send nothing, record nothing), \fB\-\-for\-real\fR (file the items, send the digest,
record the requests as reported), or \fB\-\-to\-dev\fR (a test send of the digest to FLEET_DEV_EMAIL only; no items are filed).
With none it prints a usage message and exits 2 without doing anything, and two that contradict each other are refused the same way.
.SH OPTIONS
A shell argument, matched exactly. Any other argument is refused.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Judge the new requests and render the digest. The mailbox is read and the model
is called, but nothing is filed in Jira, nothing is sent and nothing is recorded.
The work directory under
.B state/
is kept so the digest can be read; it holds request text, so delete it when done.
.TP
.B \-\-for\-real
File the Kanban items, send the digest to the lane's recipients, and record the
requests as reported so tomorrow's digest does not list them again.
.TP
.B \-\-to\-dev
Mail the digest to
.B FLEET_DEV_EMAIL
only, subject prefixed [DEV TEST]. No items are filed and nothing is recorded.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SUPPLIER_ADDRESS
The supplier-request address. Unset: the lane does nothing.
.TP
.B SUPPLIER_TO
.TQ
.B SUPPLIER_ALLOW_TO
Recipients and the allowlist they are checked against. No fallback.
.TP
.B SUPPLIER_MODEL
The model alias or id that judges each request. Unset: every request is Unsure.
.TP
.B SUPPLIER_JIRA_PROJECT
The project for the Kanban items; it must also be in
.BR JIRA_ALLOW_CREATE .
.TP
.B SUPPLIER_JIRA_TYPE
The issue type (default Task).
.TP
.B SUPPLIER_JIRA_STATUS
The status a new item is moved to after it is filed (default To Do), so it
shows on the board and not in a person's backlog. Set and empty leaves it in
the workflow's first status. A move that fails is a warning: the item exists.
.TP
.B SUPPLIER_OWNER_EMAIL
The Jira user the items are assigned to. An unknown user leaves them unassigned.
.TP
.B SUPPLIER_BOARD_URL
.TQ
.B SUPPLIER_BOARD_NAME
The board's https link and what the digest calls it.
.TP
.B SUPPLIER_QUESTION
.TQ
.B SUPPLIER_MEANING
.TQ
.B SUPPLIER_TPRM
.TQ
.B SUPPLIER_UNSURE_TEXT
The organisation's own wording for the question, what a Yes means, the risk
process, and what an Unsure item says. Generic defaults apply.
.TP
.B SUPPLIER_INTERNAL_DOMAINS
Comma\-separated staff mail domains besides the one in SUPPLIER_ADDRESS. A thread
is set aside as not a supplier request only when someone at one of these started it.
.TP
.B SUPPLIER_TECH_TERMS
Comma\-separated words that stop a No from standing. Unset: built\-in list; set
and empty: none.
.TP
.B SUPPLIER_FORM_TYPES
File types that may be read (default .xlsx). Names that look like a tax or bank
form are refused whatever the type.
.TP
.B MAILBOX_DIGEST_SENDERS
The address the mail filter's quarantine digest comes from, shared with the mailbox cleanup. Mail from it with an "End User Digest" subject is left out of the requests and counted in the digest. Unset: nothing is skipped.
.TP
.B SUPPLIER_WINDOW_DAYS
How far back to look for requests with a new message (default 3). A conversation is read whole, back 21 days before that, so a request is judged with the earlier message that carries its form.
.TP
.B FLEET_SUPPLIER_TIME
When the installer pins the timer, in
.BR FLEET_TIMEZONE .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The digest was sent (or rendered, for
.BR \-\-dry\-run ), or there was nothing new.
.TP
.B 1
cti\-supplier or cti\-mailer failed, a binary is missing, or one or more Kanban
items could not be filed. In the last case the digest still went out and the
requests were recorded; the problem is in the journal and the failure alert.
.TP
.B 2
No mode was given, or an unknown argument.
.SH EXAMPLES
Rehearse today's requests:
.PP
.EX
sudo cti\-agent run\-supplier \-\-dry\-run
.EE
.PP
Send the digest to yourself first:
.PP
.EX
sudo cti\-agent run\-supplier \-\-to\-dev
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cti\-supplier (1),
.BR cti\-mailer (1),
.BR cti\-jira (1)
